      "id": "calls[0]/system",
      "type": "system_prompt",
      "kind": "value",
      "label": "System prompt",
      "value": "You work one task with the Cipher Crack plugin's tools. Every file a tool saves goes into your workspace; paths you pass to tools are relative to it.\n\nTask: Find the key a case's message was enciphered with and read the message.\nThe case holds a message enciphered by moving every letter on by a fixed amount. Spaces were left alone, so the lengths of the words are the lengths of the real words. The key is the letter that says how far: A leaves a letter alone, B moves it on by one, and so on to Z.\nRead the message with read_cipher. Then work through the keys with decrypt: it reports what the message says under any key you ask for, and tells you nothing about whether that key is the right one. Exactly one of the twenty-six keys turns the message into English; every other key turns it into nonsense. Decide which one reads as English.\nSubmit the case as the task gave it, the key letter, and the message exactly as decrypt returned it under that key. Copy the message rather than retyping it: a single wrong letter is a wrong answer, and the key you submit must be the one that produces the message you submit.\n\nWhen the task is done, call submit with its result.",
      "parent": "calls[0]"
    },
